# Grepping for a needle in a haystack
>In this challenge, I've put a hundred thousand lines of text into the /challenge/data.txt file. grep it for the flag!

## Solve:
- I first read through the challenge and understood the syntax for grep.Then implemented it to find flag. 
```
bash
hacker@commands~grepping-for-a-needle-in-a-haystack:~$ grep pwn.college /challenge/data.txt
pwn.college{opr_Amlcm1Ijyzgu24Ps1p-ox3H.QX3EDO0wiM4ETOwIzW}
```
## Flag
```
put{opr_Amlcm1Ijyzgu24Ps1p-ox3H.QX3EDO0wiM4ETOwIzW}
```

## Concepts Learnt
- Cat command is not always useful due to size of some text
- Grep is used to find a certain text in thousands of line.

